2186045417] [17592186068825 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186302301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068825 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186400916 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068825 #edb/ref 1039 "Solving a \"Less Than\" Inequality Given the Graph of the Corresponding Parabola" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068825 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186068675 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068825 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "fc419917-fe34-5bf9-8bf0-1b022fce11ff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186069761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1045 "Solving Quadratic Inequalities From Graphs" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186069655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186049428 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186068993 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "75b8321b-47ce-5d18-b03b-4a28719bcaba" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069177 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186289999 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069177 #edb/ref 1069 "q-24351" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069177 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069177 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/09/098189dc8e96b01cb045a198eef3f00ba2df6594fc14675cad81246fc2d25964.png)\n\nGiven the graph above, solve the inequality $(x+2)(x-3)\\ge 0.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069177 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ffe39127-4650-5f93-972b-bb5efc38f550" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069177 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that our inequality\n\n$$\n(x+2)(x-3)\\ge 0\n$$\n\nis a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny=(x+2)(x-3)\n$$\n\nis *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis. We mark these values of $x$ in blue in the diagram below.\n\n![](images/3e/3e80a6e08ccff87314e5081a08332f0de508f6db02446742d1c93416d41a4b3c.png)\n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069655 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069656 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069655 #edb/ref 1061 18527 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069655 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b8c84c90-fff3-5ec0-8816-e41fb5b44431" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069655 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069656 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069760 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069656 #edb/ref 1061 18528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069656 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7efd913e-aaa5-5399-80ff-5b2b175349ec" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069656 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068751 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069758 #edb/ref 1061 37410 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069758 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "6df23a8b-1690-5d8c-8f65-086b0c58b4a4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069758 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068823 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069759 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069761 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069759 #edb/ref 1061 37567 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069759 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cc9b98d3-5b55-5a89-969d-d72ba706ab6b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069759 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186069994 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069760 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069759 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069760 #edb/ref 1061 37568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069760 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "f6eaab57-6262-53e0-95b6-d71e2ca519b4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069760 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069761 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186069758 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069761 #edb/ref 1061 37569 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069761 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d197c412-e6cd-5343-90ad-50aa69c262b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069761 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186068825 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069970 #edb/ref 1064 "A **quadratic inequality** is an inequality that involves a quadratic expression. We can often solve quadratic inequalities using a graphical method.\n\nFor example, suppose we want to find the solution to the quadratic inequality \n\n$$\nx^2+2x-3 \\geq 0.\n$$\n\nLet's consider the graph of the corresponding parabola $y=x^2+2x-3,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/c0/c04ccf6db68a0e37663fecda4c2fb68ce12dc2a02821af45a6dcad73deeb7bc3.png)\n\nOur inequality is a \"*greater than or equal to*\" inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola is *above* the $x$-axis or *touches* this axis\n\nUsing the graph above, we notice that our parabola has roots at $x=-3$ and $x=1.$ The parabola is above the $x$-axis to the left of $x=-3$ and the right of $x=1,$ as shown below. \n\n![](images/2d/2d1574ed8172f5b307e080c86b712a5e2d3a206dee0d74a797f692e9e9ae8731.png)\n\nTherefore $y = x^2+2x-3 \\geq 0$ when\n\n$$\nx \\leq -3 \\quad \\text{or} \\quad x \\geq 1,\n$$\n\nwhich is our solution.\n\n**Important:** Since we have a \"greater than *or equal to*\" inequality, the roots of the parabola are *included* in the solution set." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069970 #edb/ref 1065 3343 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069970 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "7acbb382-158e-505a-a4fe-5598239a21dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069970 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069994 #edb/ref 1064 "Suppose we want to find the solution to the quadratic inequality\n\n$$\nx^2+x-6 <  0.\n$$\n\nWe first plot the graph of the corresponding parabola $y=x^2+x-6,$ shown below.\n\n![](images/c3/c30f81cbbe79d6b54f63070c5ea161fc94488413f893a80c3e451ed6a042b187.png)\n\nNotice that our inequality is a \"*less than*\" ($<$) inequality. Therefore, we need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola is *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nThe graph above shows that our parabola has roots at $x=-3$ and $x=2.$ Moreover, the parabola lies below the $x$-axis for all values of $x$ that lie between $x=-3$ and  $x=2.$ \n\n![](images/bd/bdef6fd120108576e48a4ac495abab327dc5e9c3bbe26d007724285a9d7d84a1.png)\n\nTherefore, $x^2+x-6 <0$ when\n\n$$\n-3 < x < 2,\n$$\n\nwhich is our solution.\n\n**Important:** Since our inequality is a \"*less than*\" inequality, the roots of the parabola are *not* included in the solution set." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069994 #edb/ref 1065 6197 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069994 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "772a47c1-c2f0-54ee-a7c4-61d24a65bb87" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186069994 #edb/ref 1067 "Strict Inequalities" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288167 #edb/ref 1080 "x\\ge 3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288167 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288167 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1383fd97-77d3-5ac2-be23-4b9d7dc8885a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288395 #edb/ref 1080 "-3\\le x\\le 2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288395 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288395 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "362fcbae-cb89-5509-8424-b1ee7253363f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288519 #edb/ref 1080 "$x\\le -2$ or $x\\ge 3$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288519 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288519 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "46d5b3e6-49b1-5f02-8bd8-ebc685df8719" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288534 #edb/ref 1080 "-2\\le x\\le 3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288534 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288534 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "4881613a-3587-5b83-92d1-c4557759480e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288635 #edb/ref 1080 "x\\le -2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288635 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288635 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "570c0835-b65c-52fe-9f64-104b4ace6481" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288395 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288534 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288635 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186288167 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289999 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "7a561c7b-ae6b-533f-be16-6d5b7c106d68" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
